/-! ## (5.5) with an arbitrary cutoff

The near/far split of `R_2^-` works for any cutoff, not just `brsCutScale r`.
Taking a cutoff that is constant on each dyadic window `I_k` is what allows the
near part to be compared with the fixed-scale truncated kernel. -/

